OL,3,AMinisters ask public for views on      
OL,4,Achanging age of consent                
OL,6,FThe government is inviting the public  
OL,7,Fto share its views as ministers        
OL,8,Fconsider whether or not to stagger the 
OL,9,Fage of consent.                        
OL,11,FCurrently adults of any age are legally
OL,12,Fable to have sex with 16 and           
OL,13,F17-year-olds, however some campaigners 
OL,14,Fhave argued that different limits      
OL,15,Fshould apply, depending on the age gap 
OL,16,Fbetween the people involved.           
OL,18,FPrime Minister Andy Burnham said he    
OL,19,Fwanted survivors, parents, young       
OL,20,Fpeople, victim support services and the
OL,21,Fwider public to "to share their        
OL,22,Fexperiences and inform this process".  
OL,23,APub: 24-NovQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2 
